 "notes": "Multi-state paper: only the South Carolina part was recorded (pages 7-26 left column). Plate 1 (page 1) and pages 26-29 describe Arkansas and the New Madrid seismic zone and were not recorded. Rincon, Ga. exposure (fig. 10) not recorded. Q1 is OCR 'Ql' on page 9 (read as Q1, inferred). Soil horizons (A, E, Bh, B-C, C) of the humods are described in general on page 11 (Bh 0.5-1.5 m; base of Bh generally 0.6 to 1 m below land surface, page 25) and are not stored as units. Sand-blow site labels BR, AR, RRR, CH, FM, WV, SAN, OL, SOPO, MYRB, McL are named without locations and were not stored. Radiocarbon ages of basal Bh at HW are 5,000 to 10,000 years (page 25, Weems and others, 1986). Table 1 (page 10) is a generic liquefaction susceptibility table from Youd and Perkins (1978) and was not recorded. SUBSURFACE: source sands that liquefied generally occur within 3 to 10 m depth (page 11); no unit tops or bases with elevations.",
